# Opening Settings' Wi-Fi pane, so that something asks the radio to scan.
#
# iOS lists networks only while the Wi-Fi pane is open: wifid asks apple80211 for a scan, the
# reference implementation's lx layer hands it to ath11k, the firmware answers. The pane is opened
# by libredwood-sb.dylib, which answers the notification com.redwood.wifi by asking LaunchServices
# for "App-Prefs:root=WIFI" (src/inject_sb.c).
#
# The notification is posted by a program of its own after a `sleep`, not by rwtouch's own `wait`:
# `rwtouch wait 25 notify com.redwood.wifi` printed its command line and then never came back
# (wifiscan3, 13:51), while `sleep 40` followed by `rwtouch notify` is exactly what rc.jobs.lang
# does and it is answered every time.
#
# 30 s is after SpringBoard has its icons; 60 s more keeps the run alive while the pane scans.
sleep 30
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.redwood.wifi
sleep 60
/redwood/bin/rwtouch notify com.redwood.wifi
sleep 40
